{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/713993-can-a-solar-fail-to-master-a-human-ability","id":713993,"title":"Can a Solar Fail to Master a Human Ability?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-22T01:42:40-07:00","id":713993,"title":"Can a Solar Fail to Master a Human Ability?","content":"I realize that OOC, the player can distribute attributes, abilities, and charms as they desire. This is a question about how Solars work within the setting.<br /> <br /> Let's imagine a Solar Dawn named Unfurling Steel Blossom. She's a graceful dancer and fighter able to carve a deadly path through her enemies. She has a Zenith circle-mate named Harmonious Mountain can dive into lava, trek tirelessly for weeks through frozen lands, and shrugs off the blows of a dozen men like they're bug bites. <br /> <br /> One day, Unfurling Steel decides that whole 'shrug off mighty blows' thing sounds interesting. Harmonious Mountain agrees to teach her the exercises and techniques he learned as a young monk/goat herder on the misty slopes of Mount Terrimungu.<br /> <br /> Is it possible that after weeks/months of diligent effort, Unfurling Sterl Blossom is unable to internalize these techniques? She becomes a bit more hardy, but no more so than a hale and weathered mortal?<br /> <br /> Again, I'm not asking if it's 'okay' for this to happen at a table. I know that this is completely up to players.<br /> <br /> Given what we're told of Solars, however, is it possible that Unfurling Steel Blossom <i><b>simply can't</b></i> become that hearty and resistant? It's just a limit she'll have to live with outside of external magical forces or the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T01:52:12-07:00","id":714024,"title":"","content":"I'd say it's possible. Maybe not because the Solar can fail to understand the technique, but because they can fail to invest enough work and attention into it. Learning patience, for example, is something that takes effort and a willingness to change as a person, which isn't necessarily something Solars are great at (Solars sometimes being impatient, cruel, inattentive or having other character flaws are after all one of the staples of what makes them interesting). You could justify it at the table with how the particular technique requires some certain mindset or personality.<br /> <br /> That's not to say Solars <i>can't</i> overcome their personal flaws, of course - they obviously can - but this also seems to be the one area where they can fail, and fail spectacularly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2196-riklurt","name":"Riklurt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T02:11:57-07:00","id":714037,"title":"","content":"This... is an arguable one.<br /> <br /> Personally, I fairly firmly say that yes, a Solar <i>can </i>fail to get better. But that's based on how I view Exaltation, and I'd require a good reason for it. Exaltation reflects qualities already within the person. A great musician becomes sublime, the fast duellist becomes even faster. If you lack that quality to start with, you can build on it... but no more than a mortal can. If Unfurling Steel Blossom grew up on the streets, and already was a bit tough, I'd say she can improve and learn her friend's techniques, at least to a degree. If she grew up in a life of privilage and simply isn't that tough... training does no more for her than it does a mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T02:15:02-07:00","id":714038,"title":"","content":"I'd say yes, narratively there's no reason, despite their penchant for superhuman excellence, why all Solars should excel at everything. Some people just don't have much talent in certain areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T02:27:21-07:00","id":714044,"title":"","content":"In general, Solar Exaltation enhances abilities and talents the person in question already had. Yes, a Solar can undoubtely learn and master new abilities, and overcome their weaknesses, but only if they had a possibility of doing this in them already. There are things that simply cannot be learned if you don't have the inherent qualities for them. Some of those qualities can be partially gained through the hard work, but mastery often requires something more.<br /> <br /> TL/DR: Solar Exaltation may be enough to allow Solars to become <i>competent</i> in any field they might desire, but i doubt it is enough to allow for mastery unless the seeds were there from the beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T02:49:17-07:00","id":714062,"title":"","content":"I've talked in favour of this before in response to questions of immediate adaptations, but considering in the long term...<br /> <br /> A few days ago, while browsing through Youtube, I saw a thumbnail to a video that seemed to be depicting some kind of anime scene in which a character was dancing. It set me off on a train of thought about how much anime, and media in general, might contain imagery or characterisations that I would find striking or compelling, as well as the possibilities of actually dancing, that I will never intersect with because there's just too much to be encompassed in a single human life. That also got me to thinking of depictions of enormous libraries (such as the Duke's Archives in Dark Souls), and how no one person could read everything in them.<br /> <br /> It made me think about what it would be like to be able to live a lot longer; to have the <i>time</i> for so much more.<br /> <br /> It's come to be part of my image for what the possibilities of a Solar's lifespan are; not necessarily about learning everything (certainly unlikely to get 5 in all Abilities), but the idea of breadth and permutations, of expanding yourself laterally. A person who spent several centuries reading an entire library. I find it more engaging and comprehensible than the idea of a Solar who somehow expands the one ability beyond the usual boundaries, this idea of a person who cannot relate to anybody.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would actually think that such breadth means you can relate to <i>even more</i> people; your interests and experiences can expand to include things that even more people would share with you, and your life is long enough to actually do that sharing. Sure, the short-lived people in question are only ever experiencing a tiny fraction of your life, but really, that's the case for their interactions with one another as well.<br /> <br /> And even with all of that, the Solar is still so small...<br /> <br /> As an answer to the original question, this is all something that leads me to think: &quot;eventually&quot;. If she needed to relocate herself to his homeland and try to absorb an approximation of his formative experiences to really get it, it's something she would be far better equipped for than any mortal.<br /> <br /> (This is in no way me saying that any player who wants their character to build up Resistance 5 and associated Charms needs to have a lifetime of conditioning for it, it's more of an expansive setting thing)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T03:06:47-07:00","id":714070,"title":"","content":"We actually have an example of a Solar that struggled with mastering human ability. Her name was Brigid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T03:21:12-07:00","id":714081,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's possible for a Solar to fail to master the charms inherent to their nature. It might be that the Dawn needs to learn the charms her way, of course. Ex3 is big individualized power. Brigid exists as a legend, and possibly as a one-off. I don't think anything in the setting itself is bettered by extending this concept past her.<br /> <br /> That being said, if a player WANTS that to be part of their story, the desire of the player for a certain narrative should take precedence over the internal consistency of the setting. It's no different than a ST allowing a PC Dragon-Blooded Sorcerer to seek and attain initiation into CCS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T03:29:45-07:00","id":714095,"title":"","content":"I'd say yes they can fail, but not for long if they push it. Just bringing it back to the game mechanics.<br /> Any mortal, if unskilled will absolutely fail a task.<br /> A Solar, on the other hand, can at least try. I mean, yes, the chances you'll succeed the 2 difficulty roll on 2 dots is fairly low but it can happen. That you can channel your virtues and motes, increases the possibility.<br /> <br /> But that's for one task. Mastery implies the capability to generate a result reliably over and over.<br /> <br /> So, same mortal wants to master an ability. How does he do it? In game terms, expend XP. Or storywise, he devotes his time and effort on training that ability. But then again, mortals don't really get that much XP do they? Since their daily lives revolve on the mundane and not dying, it may take their whole lives to get enough XP. Also there's that dying thing, a mortal's gotta survive first and that's not easy.<br /> <br /> Now, Solar dude over there wants to train the same thing. But this time, his live revolves around the epic and legendary. Even if he doesn't do anything AMAZING for decades, he gets more XP out of just existing and going about his life. Then the fact that he can expect to live longer, devote more time to personal pleasures, and just all around have more free time than any mortal.<br /> Then it just boils down to economics. How much XP does he bank, and how does he spend it? If he wants to be MASTER CHEF, Lord of Falafels, but consistently spends all his points into The Art of Making Flatulence an Acceptable Musical Instrument, then that's failure right there.<br /> And again, he doesn't even have to spend the same XP as the mortal. He can spend motes just to make himself better, and no one's gonna fault him for that.<br /> <br /> tl;dr: Yes but no with minimal effort and guts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3364-sodina","name":"sodina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T03:30:27-07:00","id":714096,"title":"","content":"I would be surprised if the story of Brigid was not changed in the new Edition to reflect matters of personality rather than difficulty with Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T03:50:51-07:00","id":714113,"title":"","content":"It seems like the &quot;techniques&quot; described in the OP would be akin to like...the training some monks undergo in order to meditate under freezing cold waterfalls? Am I wrong there?<br /> <br /> The Solar may not grok something like that, sure, but that is purely a narrative thing. She may not have the patience to learn all the (mortal) ways to become toughened against elemental exposure. If she trains endurance, she may still never be able to take hits onto her bare skin with iron rods without flinching, solely relying on mortal training to see her through it. <br /> <br /> But that of course doesn't mean she is forever unable to manifest something like Iron Kettle Body. That's the privilege of being Exalted. in mechanical terms, maybe she can train Resistance, but always had fairly poor Stamina, so she's unlikely to be as good as her Circlemate unless she devotes XP to both. Solely devoting to Reaistance and Resistance Charms will get you pretty far when you use the Charms, but when you're not, you won't be as good as the person whose natural Stamina is 3 points higher.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/713993-can-a-solar-fail-to-master-a-human-ability?p=714044#post714044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, Solar Exaltation enhances abilities and talents the person in question already had. Yes, a Solar can undoubtely learn and master new abilities, and overcome their weaknesses, but only if they had a possibility of doing this in them already. There are things that simply cannot be learned if you don't have the inherent qualities for them. Some of those qualities can be partially gained through the hard work, but mastery often requires something more.<br /> <br /> TL/DR: Solar Exaltation may be enough to allow Solars to become <i>competent</i> in any field they might desire, but i doubt it is enough to allow for mastery unless the seeds were there from the beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/713993-can-a-solar-fail-to-master-a-human-ability?p=714037#post714037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you lack that quality to start with, you can build on it... but no more than a mortal can. If Unfurling Steel Blossom grew up on the streets, and already was a bit tough, I'd say she can improve and learn her friend's techniques, at least to a degree. If she grew up in a life of privilage and simply isn't that tough... training does no more for her than it does a mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im not sure what you two are saying.<br /> <br /> What I think I'm reading is something like, &quot;if the Solar had Stamina 2 and Reaistance 0, and grew up in a palace, they're not allowed to use XP to buy Resistance 5 and associated progressive Charms?&quot;<br /> <br /> If that's what you're saying, why? If that's not what you're saying, then I'm not sure what you ARE saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 10-22-2015, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T04:05:49-07:00","id":714128,"title":"","content":"My favourite characters have been defined by their weaknesses and ineptitudes as much as their strengths. However useful it might be for my pampered noble scholar to learn Survival and Athletics or my cheerfully ignorant Modern Earth Aspect superhero to learn Occult, they will never do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T05:34:48-07:00","id":714227,"title":"","content":"Part of me agrees with Isator that Exalts have a relatively-unique opportunity to devote decades or even lifetimes to develop their skills, but I also feel inclined to point out that for the most part, the distinction is academic; most Exalts won't experience those tens of decades, and even the ones that do are just as likely as the rest of us to have crises of faith in which they wonder if all the effort they're sinking into it is &quot;worth it.&quot; It's <i>very</i> possible for them to never master a skill, even when they <i>really</i> want to.<br /> <br /> My own example: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Shichirou was my first Exalted character, and before the game imploded he'd spent about forty in-game years as an Exalt. He always saw himself as a brawler, but wanted to be a martial artist (ignoring 2e rolling the two into one Ability; even in my early days I thought the idea of a martial art built around &quot;fighting like a Solar&quot; was dumb). His father was a martial artist, his rivals and enemies were martial artists, and he was fascinated with the idea of the deeper truths hidden deep in the styles. <br /> <br /> He had plenty of opportunities; one of the first places his circle visited was a Gold Faction manse with a magical AI and a dojo; he wrestled with Jade Mountain Stylists, Orgiastic Fugitives, and Fire Dragons alike; later he even had the opportunity to learn Sidereal Martial Arts! <br /> <br /> Still, every time, he looked at the opportunity offered, and said, &quot;Sorry, I got shit to do.&quot; (Even taking into account that a <i>huge</i> chunk of that forty years was spent either in training or training others!)<br /> <br /> In my headcanon, wherever he's gone, he's still a brawler.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-22-2015, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T05:55:00-07:00","id":714254,"title":"","content":"I am adverse to saying that, mechanically, a player cannot take a dot in an Ability or Attribute, or purchase a Charm (provided they follow the Charm tree). Narratively, though, it's hard to take somebody seriously when they say Blooming Onion Master wants to raise his resistance to pain, but does no training to show his commitment. If it was something like Drum Master Pickles trying to make himself more Temperant by quitting drinking (at least, to excess), but he has an Addiction to alcohol.... that honestly does take a while to get over.It's not imppossible.... it just takes longer for that particular Solar to quit drinking than a different Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T05:57:01-07:00","id":714256,"title":"","content":"I'm personally of the belief that anyone could potentially learn anything, given previous knowledge and skills to build it on. I therefore do believe that as one develops, options are in fact cut off, if only because your body changes and your mind has chosen paths that, while leading towards many worthwhile perspectives, lead away from others. Given infinite time, one <i>might</i> be able to learn everything, but I'd think one would start forget previous knowledge way before that.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, a Solar can buy dots in every Ability she wishes to without restriction or condition. Narratively, there are reasons for every Ability she has at 0. Mostly, it's probably that she hasn't need of it, but it could also be that she's uninterested, actively opposed to it, or maybe just can't seem to get it. These descriptions don't prevent you from putting some dots in those Abilities later, which would be a great break-through for the character.<br /> <br /> In short, I think it's unhelpful to think of what a Solar can do, because a Solar is such a classifying and mechanical term. Instead, what your character can and can't do is up to how you imagine her, which influences her stats, which in turn influences how you imagine her. Some Solars are probably able to learn everything. Some, for some reason, probably are not. It's not really something that benefits from being decided on a category level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 10-22-2015, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T06:02:14-07:00","id":714268,"title":"","content":"When it comes to Caste and Favored Abilities, an Exalt will always be able to master those, barring extremely unusual circumstances (Brigid). It's just the magical benefit of Exaltation. Even if a Solar was completely illiterate prior to Exaltation, if Linguistics were one of his Caste Abilities, he'd be able to master writing and languages.<br /> <br /> But non-Caste, non-Favored Abilities, a Solar is no better at picking those up than any mortal and could find himself struggling to get good at that Ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-22-2015, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T06:06:20-07:00","id":714287,"title":"","content":"A lot of these arguments sound like &quot;I'm choosing for my character not to do this,&quot; or &quot;I'm choosing not to spend XP on this,&quot; which is different from &quot;they're actually physically or mentally unable to do this.&quot; <br /> <br /> It's weird mashing up the narrative aspect (&quot;he's incapable of doing so&quot;) with the mechanical (&quot;I choose to spend XP elsewhere&quot;). A Solar swordsman PC has no obstacle preventing her from raining to Resistance 5, but that still requires a lot of effort (and OOC, a lot of CP that the player might blanch at), so the player stops at a rating of 3 where they can buy all the Resistance Charms they really want, fluffs it as &quot;I really have no interest in going even harder at Yu-Sham CrossFit&quot; and maybe the player goes back to it later or maybe not. <br /> <br /> For a pure NPC, even then it flows more from &quot;this is the role of the NPC in the story and these are her personality and goals. It would take something monumentally disruptive to her life for her to get into Survival training, let alone become puissant at at...in other words, she could dabble in learning it if it was literally a matter of life or death, but that's just exceptionally unlikely, and it's even less likely she would ever achieve the kind of mastery represented by a 5.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 10-22-2015, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T06:06:28-07:00","id":714288,"title":"","content":"Caveat, Weimann - Mechanically, a <i>PC</i> can blah blah blah. PCs work differently, NPCs don't use XP, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T06:22:48-07:00","id":714305,"title":"","content":"I don't really see the discrepancy, except for NPCs using different mechanical systems than the ones I mentioned. It's still a matter of how you choose to interpret a lack of dots in an Ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T06:23:31-07:00","id":714309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/713993-can-a-solar-fail-to-master-a-human-ability?p=714288#post714288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caveat, Weimann - Mechanically, a <i>PC</i> can blah blah blah. PCs work differently, NPCs don't use XP, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>An NPC Solar could probably do anything (as in , has no hard restriction preventing it), but there the question turns on &quot;given the character's personality and goals, would they develop this skill?&quot; It's reasonable for Marn Mountain-Suplexer to learn Resistance to go with his Brawl and Athletics especially as he doesn't wear armor, but for Seven-Petaled Rose Pearl, courtesan-spy extraordinaire of the Ninety-Nine Seraglios, she may balk at the thought of lifting weights and doing squats unless she really, really needs to. Speaking of, she just learned of a great wonder at the bottom of the lava-filled Fire Stomach Lake and won't tell anyone else about it, so she might start training to dive down there personally and get it before someone else finds out and does the same. Even if she simultaneously worries about how bulking up with muscle* in order to learn Element-Resisting Prana might affect her silhouette when wearing only a few veils later in the week, or how living naked in the desert to harden her exposure to the elements might unduly dry out her skin and give it the unpleasant tan of a servant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T06:40:24-07:00","id":714352,"title":"","content":"I often find characters are more interesting for the things they can't do, rather than what they can. Specifically, the reasons behind why they can't do them. I'd be all for a player deciding that no matter what, their character can't do X or Y.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8752-don-raccoon","name":"Don Raccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8752_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T09:35:14-07:00","id":714697,"title":"","content":"I would say...<br /> <br /> If a Solar really puts their heart and mind to something, they can master it, whatever it is. That said, most Solars, like most humans, are not going to try to master just anything. They will have specific focuses, drives, and reservations that will keep them on one track at the expense of others.<br /> <br /> In other words, a Solar should never face situation where they <i>really, really </i>want to learn to do something, and <i>really, really </i>try to master it, but just cannot for... some reason. There will be plenty of situations where they just won't be willing to go the distance, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T10:13:00-07:00","id":714726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/713993-can-a-solar-fail-to-master-a-human-ability#post713993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given what we're told of Solars, however, is it possible that Unfurling Steel Blossom <i><b>simply can't</b></i> become that hearty and resistant? It's just a limit she'll have to live with outside of external magical forces or the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. The Exaltation is a miracle, and sometimes the gods give miracles with their left hands. I doubt the Unconquered Sun is going to be moved to tears that one of his Chosen can parry a volcano with her sword but not her face.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T10:16:45-07:00","id":714733,"title":"","content":"I would say, absolutely, that NPC Solars, as well as any sort of supernatural, can simply have no native talent to cultivate. They will be able to achieve a low level of skill, but nothing profound. The ability to advance indefinitely to the limits of mastery is a player character perk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8507-gilgamesh","name":"Gilgamesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T10:16:56-07:00","id":714736,"title":"","content":"I have to head to work, but I'd like to say that I've read through the thread and am enjoying the diversity of answers thus far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T10:34:43-07:00","id":714765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/713993-can-a-solar-fail-to-master-a-human-ability?p=714038#post714038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say yes, narratively there's no reason, despite their penchant for superhuman excellence, why all Solars should excel at everything. Some people just don't have much talent in certain areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is the much cooler way to run things then the alternative. I think you should be able to tell the story about a Solar that always wanted to be a swordsman but kept failing due to terrible reflexes and hand-eye coordination, however persevering he uses his knowledge of crafts to create a magical paired set of glasses and sword that let him overcome his shortcomings. Saying that all Solars are capable of mastering everything shuts down a lot of potential stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T10:38:05-07:00","id":714767,"title":"","content":"Yeah, of course, sometimes things just don't click for some people.<br /> <br /> That's not anything I see Solar Exaltation as circumventing. For me, Charms (and even skills) come from inspiration, and &quot;flow&quot;, and I don't see it as necessary or desirable really to say that Exaltation makes that guaranteed, rather than that more being a quality within (or not!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T11:18:24-07:00","id":714811,"title":"","content":"I don't think human beings have the ability to develop the level of universal aptitude in real life that would be represented by having five dots in every Ability. Even the best and the brightest polymaths are only able to achieve so much in the spread of Abilities they're able to master\u2014eventually, you're going to not be good at something, and moreover, you're going to be bad at learning it. <br /> <br /> It'd be easy enough to say that Exaltation removes that limitation. I don't think that's a good idea. The &quot;dehumanizing&quot; effect, where suddenly every Exalt in Creation is a potential omnicompetent master without any of the human personality traits or flaws that intrinsically limit that, detracts from verisimilitude\u2014plus, it basically never comes up. How many characters, player or NPC, have you seen with Charms from all twenty-five abilities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T11:21:12-07:00","id":714815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/713993-can-a-solar-fail-to-master-a-human-ability#post713993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given what we're told of Solars, however, is it possible that Unfurling Steel Blossom <i><b>simply can't</b></i> become that hearty and resistant? It's just a limit she'll have to live with outside of external magical forces or the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're asking if it is possible that a particular Solar might suffer from a kind of metaphysical limitation not otherwise experienced by other Solars, which makes it objectively impossible to learn something that ought to fall within their realm of capability? My instinct is to say &quot;no&quot;. But this comes with several caveats:<br /> <br /> 1. It's your game. You can always make an exception, if you think it makes the story better.<br /> 2. There is a difference between difficulty and impossibility. It can absolutely be more difficult for one Solar to master a particular set of abilities than it is for another Solar to master the same set, and it's absolutely believable that if s/he simply finds it very difficult and time consuming to learn, s/he may opt to stop trying entirely and then justify giving up by deciding that the difficulty = impossibility. People do this all the time, and Solars are people (see: Luke and Yoda in the swamp with the X-Wing).<br /> <br /> In other words: no, I do not think that there are flawed Solar Exaltations floating around which are metaphysically incapable of imparting mastery of things within their realm of potential. But I do think that there are <i>Solars </i>running around who might be <i>psychologically unwilling</i> to push past the difficulty of mastering things which are harder for them than others.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T11:28:16-07:00","id":714830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/713993-can-a-solar-fail-to-master-a-human-ability?p=714811#post714811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many characters, player or NPC, have you seen with Charms from all twenty-five abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll start by pointing at DotFA <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> While also saying that this is a bit hyperbolic, since I really haven't read this thread to be about casual universal hypercompetency so much as Exalts having that potential, if they choose, at least in the context of a white room. Chances are that 99.9% of Exalts will neither live long enough to do that not be interested in doing it even if they do live long enough. And the maybe 1 Exalt who does will teuly be a jack of all trades but master of none...or a GMPC sue, as he case may be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T11:31:59-07:00","id":714834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/713993-can-a-solar-fail-to-master-a-human-ability?p=714830#post714830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll start by pointing at DotFA <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>To rephrase: how many times have you seen <i>someone play a character</i> with charms from all the abilities. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T11:58:17-07:00","id":714987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/713993-can-a-solar-fail-to-master-a-human-ability?p=714834#post714834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To rephrase: how many times have you seen <i>someone play a character</i> with charms from all the abilities. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Never, but I've also never had a game get to the XP values where that might be remotely feasible (and there was always something enter to buy in something you were already invested in, or due to not stepping on another player's toes).<br /> <br /> But like in hypothetical terms divorced from XP or the rules of the table, it could happen I think. But would still be exceedingly unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T12:07:29-07:00","id":715041,"title":"","content":"I tend to view it as a sort of aptitude and mindset thing. Like I recall at least one Abyssal in 2E who had a low martial arts rating and the explanation was just that they lacked the patience and focus needed to really be good at it.<br /> <br /> To that end I don't think its a matter of being entirely incapable of it, but I would say there are times or skills that a person just has issues with and as a result even the augmented learning ability of an exaltation means it will still take them forever to learn it just because they have to conquer embedded parts of their own psyche to be able to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T13:53:21-07:00","id":715370,"title":"","content":"Has anyone asked the question whether it's possible for a <i>human</i> to fail to master a human ability?<br /> <br /> Out of character, they're the same as Exalts - they're just as free to buy more dots in any abilities and attributes as exalts are.<br /> I'd treat them the same in-character, too. If every human can potentially master anything, then so can every Exalt.<br /> If some humans are unable to master some abilities due to lack of aptitude, then I wouldn't say Exaltation fixes that - except, <i>maybe</i>, in the case of caste abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}